' bug-441 / plan-97: a user RESOURCE MAY reuse a bare built-in resource name.
' The built-in resources are package-qualified (`fs::File`, `net::Socket`), so
' bare `File` and `Socket` no longer name builtins — they are free for user
' declarations. Each RESOURCE below names a distinct user resource, closed by the
' user's own `CLOSE BY`, and the package compiles cleanly.
'
' This supersedes bug-373's RESOURCE_SHADOWS_BUILTIN ban: under the hard cutover
' there is no shadow to refuse. The old failure mode (the built-in's close op
' dragging its runtime helper into the module while the user's `CLOSE BY` ran)
' cannot arise, because a bare name never resolves to the built-in at all.
RESOURCE File CLOSE BY demoLink::close
RESOURCE Socket CLOSE BY demoLink::finalize

LINK "sqlite3" AS demoLink
  FUNC open(path AS String) AS RES File
    SYMBOL "sqlite3_open"
    ABI (path CString, db OUT CPtr) AS status CInt32
    RETURN db
    SUCCESS_ON status = 0
  END FUNC

  FUNC close(RES db AS File) AS Nothing
    SYMBOL "sqlite3_close"
    ABI (db CPtr) AS status CInt32
    SUCCESS_ON status = 0
  END FUNC

  FUNC finalize(RES sock AS Socket) AS Nothing
    SYMBOL "sqlite3_finalize"
    ABI (sock CPtr) AS status CInt32
    SUCCESS_ON status = 0
  END FUNC
END LINK
